<title>USA: GB Airways orders two Boeing 737's.</title>
<headline>GB Airways orders two Boeing 737's.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co said Friday that British airline GB Airways has ordered two Boeing 737-300s, valued at $82 million.</p>
<p>Boeing said in a statement the 737's are the first new aircraft purchased by the company. Boeing is scheduled to deliver the airplanes in January and February 1998.</p>
<p>The new airplanes will accommodate 114 passengers and will replace two 737-200s and join a fleet of five Boeing 737-400s and three Boeing 737-200s.</p>
<p>The airline flies routes for British Airways under a franchise agreement. All aircraft are painted with the British Airways livery, and cabin crew wear the standard British Airways uniform.</p>
</text>
